Mutation proof (temporary edit, reverted before final run):
  Edited themedTrendPayload in web/static/js/insights.js to add:
    raw.data.forEach(function (t, i) { if (i < markers.length) t.marker = markers[i]; });
  before the filterTrendTraces call (assigning markers onto raw's own traces).
  Ran: node --test "web/static/js/insights-trends-cap.test.cjs"
  Result: 9 pass, 2 fail (both new tests). Failing assertion (both failures):
    AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: The expression evaluated to a falsy value:
      assert.ok(!('marker' in raw.data[i]))
    { generatedMessage: true, code: 'ERR_ASSERTION', actual: false, expected: true, operator: '==', diff: 'simple' }
  Also failed the raw-deep-equals-snapshot assert.deepEqual(raw, before) in the 5-category test (raw now carried the injected marker objects).
  Reverted the edit; diff'd against /tmp/claude-1000/th1-worker/insights.js.bak (identical) to confirm a clean revert; re-ran full suite -> 21/21 pass again.

Browser verification (Playwright, chromium-1243, --no-sandbox, 1300x900 viewport, server on :8251 via scripts/whatif-verify.sh):
Ranges: Jan-Aug = /insights?start=2026-01-01&end=2026-08-27 (41 categories total); June = /insights?start=2026-06-01&end=2026-06-30 (33 categories total).
Note: for #chart-trends, charts.js's renderChart swaps x<->y for the horizontal-bar orientation, so category labels/order live in chart.data[0].y (not .x) after render -- the verify script asserts against .y accordingly. Category-order parity checked against `#category-trends-table tbody tr:not([hidden])` data-category values in DOM order at every step; all orderOk=true, no FAIL/console.error lines printed by the harness across any range/theme/step.

